Id: dbs021w
Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_databases
Fix: Tighten PostgreSQL's configuration files to 640 root:postgres.
References: postgresql.conf(5); pg_hba.conf(5)
Controls: CIS 3.3, 5.2; NIST AC-3, IA-5(7); ISO 5.17, 8.3; CE User access control

PostgreSQL's configuration is readable past its keepers: the
connection and authentication details in postgresql.conf and
pg_hba.conf lie open to users the server never meant to have
them. Stock layouts differ, so this is a warning, not a
failure; 640 root:postgres keeps postgres reading and the rest
out.
